From 0ce1c85e6886a489b007fb034957772640f4ee6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ultras <stavultras@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 12:48:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/arm/mt7981: MT7987 PCIe Gen3 host and MT7992 Wi-Fi 7 card
 (pcie-wifi=)

The MT7987 machine gets its PCIe port 0 (0x11280000, SPI 168): a model
of the MediaTek Gen3 controller (reset/link status, configuration TLPs
through CFGNUM and the 0x1000 window, INTx, MSI capture) with QEMU's
generic PCIe root port as the RC and the slot on its secondary bus.

pcie-wifi=mt7992 puts a MediaTek MT7992 (Filogic 680) card into the
slot, a radio silent model for the unmodified mt7996e driver: BAR0 with
the L1/L2 remap windows, the WFDMA0 rings, the firmware side of the MCU
interface (patch/RAM download, UNI command results, the a-die id, chip
config and eFuse queries) and TX free events for data frames.  The
firmware needs the packages kmod-mt7996e and kmod-mt7992-firmware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 hw/arm/Kconfig                |   2 +
 hw/arm/mt7981/meson.build     |   2 +
 hw/arm/mt7981/mt7981.h        |   6 +
 hw/arm/mt7981/mt7981_router.c |  42 +++
 hw/arm/mt7981/mt7987_pcie.c   | 317 +++++++++++++++++
 hw/arm/mt7981/mt7992_wifi.c   | 641 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 1010 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/arm/mt7981/mt7987_pcie.c
 create mode 100644 hw/arm/mt7981/mt7992_wifi.c

